      "slug": "gluten",
      "term": "gluten",
      "definition": "The network of proteins formed when wheat or spelt flour is mixed with water. Gluten gives dough its elasticity and structure, trapping the gas produced by yeast. Spelt gluten is more fragile than wheat gluten and can break down if over-mixed or over-proofed."
    },
    {
      "slug": "proving",
      "term": "proving",
      "definition": "The final rest of shaped dough before baking, during which yeast produces gas that expands the loaf. Also called the final proof. The dough is ready when it has increased in volume and springs back slowly when pressed."
    }
  ],
