  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Seeded spelt tin loaf is a simple wholegrain bread with a close, tender crumb. You get deep nuttiness from the flour and a satisfying crunch from the seeds in every slice. Spelt "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "gluten",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "gluten"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is more extensible than wheat gluten, which means the dough relaxes quickly and should not be overworked."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "ingredient",
            "attrs": {
              "ingredientSlug": "spelt-flour",
              "slugGuessed": true,
              "amount": 500,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "wholegrain"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "ingredient",
            "attrs": {
              "ingredientSlug": "water",
              "amount": 340,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": "warm (about 35°C)"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "ingredient",
            "attrs": {
              "ingredientSlug": "yeast-dried",
              "amount": 5,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "ingredient",
            "attrs": {
              "ingredientSlug": "salt-table",
              "amount": 10,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "ingredient",
            "attrs": {
              "ingredientSlug": "olive-oil",
              "amount": 15,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "ingredient",
            "attrs": {
              "ingredientSlug": "sunflower-seeds",
              "amount": 40,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "plus a small handful for the top"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "ingredient",
            "attrs": {
              "ingredientSlug": "pumpkin-seeds",
              "amount": 40,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "plus a small handful for the top"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "ingredient",
            "attrs": {
              "ingredientSlug": "honey",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "for brushing the top"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mix the dough"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Weigh the wholegrain spelt flour into a large mixing bowl. Add the salt to one side and the dried yeast to the other, keeping them apart for now."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour in the olive oil and most of the warm water (reserve about 30 ml). Use your hand or a silicone spatula to bring the mix together into a rough dough, adding the reserved water if the flour feels dry. Spelt absorbs liquid faster than wheat: the dough should feel tacky but not sticky."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Tip in the sunflower seeds and pumpkin seeds. Mix until they are evenly distributed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Knead"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Turn the dough onto a lightly floured surface and knead for 8 minutes by hand. Because spelt "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "gluten",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "gluten"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is fragile, keep the kneading firm but not aggressive. The dough is ready when it feels smooth and springs back slowly when pressed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Shape the dough into a ball and return it to the bowl. Cover with a clean damp cloth and leave in a warm spot for 60 minutes, or until roughly doubled in size."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shape and prove"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Lightly grease a 900 g loaf tin with a little olive oil. Tip the dough onto a lightly floured surface. Flatten it gently into a rectangle roughly the length of the tin, then roll it up tightly from one short end. Pinch the seam closed and place seam-side down in the tin."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cover the tin loosely with oiled cling film or a damp cloth and leave to "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "prove",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "proving"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " for 45 minutes. The dough is ready when it has risen just above the rim of the tin and a finger poke leaves an indent that springs back slowly. Do not leave it longer: spelt over-proves quickly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 210°C conventional. While the oven heats, brush the top of the loaf with a little water or honey and scatter over the reserved seeds."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bake for 35 minutes. If the top darkens significantly before 35 minutes are up, tent loosely with foil."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Turn the loaf out of the tin and tap the base: it should sound hollow. If it does not, return it to the oven directly on the rack for a further 5 minutes. Cool completely on a wire rack before slicing."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Dense, heavy crumb",
              "avoid": "Avoid over-kneading the dough. Spelt gluten tears under prolonged or rough handling; 8 minutes by hand is the ceiling."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Loaf collapsed or sank",
              "avoid": "Avoid leaving the dough to prove beyond the point where it clears the tin rim. Over-proving weakens the structure and the loaf collapses in the oven."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Top crust burning before loaf is cooked",
              "avoid": "Avoid uncovering the loaf without checking the base first. Tent with foil early and check the hollow-tap test to confirm doneness."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Seeds falling off the crust",
              "avoid": "Avoid scattering seeds onto a dry surface. Brush the top with honey or water first so the seeds adhere during baking."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}